id=a52sxq_gallery_slowmo_neural
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: neural frame interpolation for Gallery slow motion (test, disabled by default)
author=kusti420
description=Runs the frame interpolation network of Samsung's Instant Slow-mo (the "v3" AIFRC model, recovered into a portable form) on the A52s Hexagon DSP. A small vendor daemon, k4neuralmpp, registers a second MPP store (ISehMppStore/k4front) next to the untouched stock one, serves the frame rate conversion pipe itself (x4: three generated frames per source pair, i.e. smooth 0.25x) and forwards every other call to the stock store. The system MPP client library is pointed at the new instance. persist.sys.k4.slowmo_neural: 1 = neural x4 (default), 2 = neural x2, 0 = stock classical pipe as in gallery_slowmo. Needs target/a52sxq/patches/gallery_slowmo. The Qualcomm AI Runtime 2.46.0 libraries (prebuilts/qairt/2.46.0) and the model (prebuilts/k4neural) are not part of the repository; the build aborts with instructions when they are missing. Disabled by a `disable` file until the engine is proven in the real player.
